								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg14214#msg14214"><img src="http://www.rodcetnife.org/Themes/classic/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://www.rodcetnife.org/index.php?topic=320.msg14214#msg14214">Re: And yet again a Top Ten guilds List</a></b><br />
									<span class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #1763 on:</b> February 03, 2005, 03:28:21 pm &#187;</span></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							When I don&#039;t care about something, I don&#039;t post in a thread saying I don&#039;t care...I just &quot;don&#039;t care&quot;.  That is kinda how not caring works.<br /><br />I wonder why people continue to read here if they don&#039;t care.  There are a gazillion other web sites which I&#039;m sure would be a lot more entertaining to someone that &quot;didn&#039;t care&quot;.<br /><br />I&#039;m not saying you do care, I&#039;m not saying you don&#039;t.  I&#039;m saying it&#039;s odd you continue to post in the Top Ten Guild list when you don&#039;t even play on the server.  There are plenty people that managed to leave the server, and the boards behind.  Would you like me to try to contact one of them to give you some tips on overcoming your obsession to visit the board?<br /><br />Some of you are very angry people.  You really need to deal with that anger.  <a href="http://www.apa.org/pubinfo/anger.html" target="_blank">http://www.apa.org/pubinfo/anger.html</a> Controlling Anger -- Before It Controls You  &quot;The instinctive, natural way to express anger is to respond aggressively&quot;<br />
						</td>
					</tr>
					<tr>
						<td valign="bottom" class="smalltext">
